claimed: intent-tier-bakeoff — build the three tiers not yet tried and put all of them on ONE table with one split. PATTERNS: function-word and phrase cues tied to classes ("could you"/"please" -> request, "shall we"/"are you free" -> proposal), which is what Linagora actually did and what targets the exact failure BM25 showed -- an intent is carried by syntax, not by topic words. KNN over example embeddings: a centroid averages a class into one point and these classes are not spherical, Other least of all, so nearest-neighbours should survive that where a mean does not. LINEAR PROBE: trained weights over frozen embeddings, gradient descent in plain Scala with no dependency -- it moves the separating plane, which a centroid cannot. Same odd/even split as Symbolic and Centroid so every row is comparable, same three numbers (coverage at a margin, agreement with gold, cost). Cascades come after, in their own lane; this one only establishes what each tier can do alone.
